#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348649 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76b2fc71-6077-57d2-ac39-901d6f2b2691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348651} {:answer/id #uuid "a52d71ad-11e6-5167-bcf8-ae65eadfa527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348652} {:answer/id #uuid "077b6f7f-3977-56c2-a61e-2543afaf0d33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348653} {:answer/id #uuid "8d50387c-39aa-54b1-9a04-77afcfb4da41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348654} {:answer/id #uuid "27b684c4-0f86-531d-a7b8-bb306117fc44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a52d71ad-11e6-5167-bcf8-ae65eadfa527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348652} :answer-field/id #uuid "81a4ed19-fa9e-523d-82be-0ca48d9baada" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348650}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "330dc0a8-da4e-5828-9634-ec3b23478b80" :question/math-academy-id "q-11977" :question/problem "The Unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/assets/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=4\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,2\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348656 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cf4fbab-da52-5514-a865-702a83935490" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348658} {:answer/id #uuid "2c924d25-019d-5259-b1db-64757a7b28e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "99" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348659} {:answer/id #uuid "164ae1b2-960d-5103-b02e-9ebe1227bd13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348660} {:answer/id #uuid "95cf073f-8f1c-5b87-897a-1aa645119a17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "102" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348661} {:answer/id #uuid "a58f241f-bd67-584f-affc-49b3fc692438" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "164ae1b2-960d-5103-b02e-9ebe1227bd13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "98" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348660} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b99cb5d-5b46-5662-b40f-34f627f37d54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ecc82082-6ef2-571d-8380-aeb406da7ee2" :question/math-academy-id "q-12279" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/assets/f24ec004411065e89b68793e32c80231c7eff6f9ff31e46bc530f78c9c270064.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot 4=14.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=5\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot (-4)=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,7\\,|\\cdot 14 \\\\  & =98.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eb72e6d-147f-53d5-9056-06e28917fe03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1eb72e6d-147f-53d5-9056-06e28917fe03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348665} :answer-field/id #uuid "f699c50d-1fc5-5085-b914-b2f3c2d62624" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b719e7f-00c5-5d80-a5cd-fc351a286629" :question/math-academy-id "q-316592" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/assets/dbda6ab548ce83f1b2c2d74cf08c2ec01ea7de089bb36f8e0c98985a432202d1.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=4\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-1)\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 3=-7.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-7\\,|\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291904 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81001409-c569-533a-a2b7-efcf7f397e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291906} {:answer/id #uuid "b98004a0-aa2b-5790-aeda-a69dda80dc0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348666}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81001409-c569-533a-a2b7-efcf7f397e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291906} :answer-field/id #uuid "f259a8c8-cae9-5672-86ca-ce9c8aca1649" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75fce5ef-ce16-54b6-beee-1ddbfa19c810" :question/math-academy-id "q-316598" :question/problem "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/assets/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-4)\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 1=-12-2=-14.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-14\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11c31dcc-393d-54d7-a1d0-1a9b0f4bf516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11c31dcc-393d-54d7-a1d0-1a9b0f4bf516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348669} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b95e50a-f902-597a-ab12-0718f1ce8489" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cbba01bc-4eb3-5032-90e4-0dfde064bcd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-316609" :question/problem "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(2,2),(5,2),(4,5).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/assets/aef99dd5276166e5c7b4fb2f716b060390b6577f2d3625dd5dc835bcec6c4856.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 3=\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-5)\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,10\\,|\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =45.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
